    "derivation": "Linear, so harmonics 0, 2 and 3 are zero and the fundamental is the phasor solution, x(t) = Re{X e^{jwt}}, SIN(0 1 1meg) -> Vin = -j, w = 2pi 1e6, M = 0.5 sqrt(L1 L2) = 1u: [R1 + jwL1, jwM; jwM, jwL2 + rl] [i(l1); i(l2)] = [Vin; 0], v(p1) = jw(L1 i(l1) + M i(l2)), v(p2) = jw(L2 i(l2) + M i(l1)), dots on each inductor's first node. Cross-checked: ngspice 44.2 `ac lin 1 1meg 1meg` on this circuit with `Vin in 0 ac 1 -90` gives every one of these phasors to 1e-15 relative, at rl=25 and rl=100. A flipped M negates v(p2) and i(l2); M = 0 moves v(p1) by 17% (rl=25) and 5% (rl=100) and zeroes v(p2). Tolerance: rtol 1e-6, above the HB GMRES tolerance (1e-7)."
